{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"A selective fusion is numerically viable: keeping both convolutions and GroupNorm calls unchanged while fusing only the final SiLU-plus-residual preserves over 99.9% of elements within tolerance and gives a small gain. Before committing it, I’m testing MIOpen’s shape autotuning because convolution algorithm choice has much more leverage than the epilogue."}}
