{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"agent_message","text":"The convolution itself is already near hardware peak on the smaller shapes. The large 768²/1024² cases are different: native GroupNorm consumes several milliseconds per stage. I’m benchmarking AITer’s dedicated HIP GroupNorm there to see whether its speed is large enough to justify a numerically corrected hybrid; I will keep the exact native path if its reduction error grows with row length."}}
