{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"agent_message","text":"AITer is roughly 7× faster on the largest normalization rows, but its multi-block reduction differs too much numerically across every group. I’m making one last targeted experiment: reproduce native GroupNorm’s likely 256-lane reduction order in Triton, then see whether modest segmentation can add parallelism without crossing tolerance. This directly targets the 768²/1024² bottleneck."}}
